(6815281, 1023755, 25787, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. It was a windy day and the hawk was riding the breezes. The redwinged blackbird would attack him periodically. I liked their shapes, especially in relationship to each other in the photo.  For me, their shapes created by their motion was the abstraction. I can understand why many don''t consider it an abstract work.  I am grateful that some do. <br/> <br/>A posthumous ribbon!  How exciting. Thank You. That''s better than a 6.0.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-07-11 07:22:04.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments. It was a windy day and the hawk was riding the breezes. The redwinged blackbird would attack him periodically. I liked their shapes, especially in relationship to each other in the photo.  For me, their shapes created by their motion was the abstraction. I can understand why many don''t consider it an abstract work.  I am grateful that some do.  A posthumous ribbon!  How exciting. Thank You. That''s better than a 6.0.', '2012-07-11 08:21:11.000000', '2012-07-11 08:22:04.000000', 0),
